  "title": "Roman Bridge at Albertville",
  "provenance": "Barrington Atlas: BAtlas 17 G2",
  "placeTypeURIs": [
    "https://pleiades.stoa.org/vocabularies/place-types/bridge"
  ],
  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory reports the location of this bridge to be at \"Ad Publicanos\". Barth\u00e9l\u00e9my argues for a Roman bridge in the vicinity of a succession of modern bridges over the Arly at Albertville, dating back to the 16th century, but does not report any associated archaeological evidence.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "A hypothesized Roman bridge over the river Arly just above its confluence with the Is\u00e9re at modern Albertville in France.",
